DOCX ends a table of contents at the next paragraph's start

Word ends a TOC field at the start of the paragraph after the last
entry: alone in an empty paragraph, or before the text that follows it.
The import keeps that paragraph inside the index only for a titled TOC
whose end stands alone; otherwise the paragraph lands after the index
section (untitled and bare TOCs, R15.11c; text or a shape after the
end, patch 0078). Writer's own TOCs have no such paragraph at all. The
export closed the field inside the last entry, and Word's Update Table
left an extra empty line after the entries (Ely R15.11k). When a
table of contents' last paragraph is not empty and a text paragraph
follows its section, DOCX now closes the field at the start of that
paragraph and keeps the paragraph inside the TOC content control; an
empty last paragraph still holds the end, as before. Other indexes
(bibliography, index) keep the old export.
testFdo77129 and testTdf121561_tocTitleDocx now expect Word's layout:
the end alone in the paragraph after the last entry, inside the
control, so the body has one paragraph fewer outside it.
